# Home Assistant Add-on: Apporo CF Tunnel Web

![Project Stage][project-stage-shield]
![Project Maintenance][maintenance-shield]

Connect an Apporo Security Access (Cloudflare Tunnel) to Home Assistant without
opening ports, with a Web GUI.

## About

Apporo CF Tunnel Web connects your Home Assistant instance through a secure
Cloudflare Tunnel, so you can reach it from the Internet without opening ports
in your router. Its Web GUI (the **Apporo Tunnel** panel) sets it up in one of
two ways:

- **Apporo Link**: sign in with your Apporo account on [www.apporo.ai][apporo]
  and connect an Apporo Security Access. Apporo provides the tunnel, its public
  hostnames and, where you turn it on, their access protection.
- **Your own Cloudflare tunnel** (the **Setup** and **Config** pages): use a
  tunnel token from the Cloudflare Dashboard, or let the add-on create a tunnel
  in your Cloudflare account. This needs a domain name (e.g. example.com) that
  uses Cloudflare for its DNS.

The add-on is a fork of WOOWTECH's Woow Cloudflared add-on, itself based on the
[Cloudflared app (add-on)][upstream] for Home Assistant.

## Disclaimer

Please make sure to be compliant with the
[Cloudflare Self-Serve Subscription Agreement][cloudflare-sssa] when using this
add-on.

